Now, about "A new strength first shows at the next update and must not shift the rhythm." - This means:
- When the user calls the returned function, it just stores the new strength
- The new strength takes effect on the next `updateAnimationManager` call
- It should NOT reset or shift the elapsed time / phase

My implementation above already handles this correctly because:
- The returned function just updates `strength` variable
- The `_update` function uses the current `strength` value at the time of the next update
- `elapsedMs` is not affected by changing strength

"Several beacons may share one manager" - This is handled because each `startBeacon` call creates its own task and adds it to the manager. Multiple tasks can coexist.

